## Feature 2: Location-Based Dashboard & Commute Search

**Description:** The core discovery engine utilizing real-world commute times rather than straight-line distance.

### Frontend User Stories
- **US2.1 (Parent):** As a parent, I want the app to automatically detect my location (falling back to address book, then last session, then manual entry) so that I immediately see schools relevant to my area.
- **US2.2 (Parent):** As a parent, I want to see dashboard tiles showing the number of available schools, open admissions, and closed admissions in my area so that I understand the current landscape at a glance.
- **US2.3 (Parent):** As a parent, I want to input my desired commute time and see an auto-calculated "Arrive By" time (e.g., 8:15 AM for an 8:30 AM start) so I know exactly when my child needs to leave home.
- **US2.4 (Parent):** As a parent, I want to filter search results by educational board (CBSE, ICSE, etc.), school age, and Total Cost of Ownership (TCO) so that I only see viable options.

### Backend User Stories
- **US2.5 (Backend):** As a system, I need to query the Google Maps Distance Matrix API using the user's coordinates and the school's coordinates, factoring in morning traffic conditions, to return accurate commute times.
- **US2.6 (Backend):** As a system, I need to aggregate fee data (tuition, transport, cafeteria, uniform, admission fees) from the database into a single TCO integer for the frontend to filter against.

